# The trial of pod-proxy in podvm: podvm-ssh takes pod-proxy with the
# feature `blocking` (a private runtime of one thread; podvm's own code stays
# synchronous). The dialer of the relay legs (`dial_ws` of mux/node.rs, for
# the node and the operator) reads the proxy of the environment once for each
# dial (`Dialer::from_environment`): `https_proxy`, `HTTPS_PROXY`,
# `all_proxy`, `ALL_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY`, by the rules of pod-proxy.
# pod-proxy decides (`blocking::Dialer::proxy_at`) and carries a dial through
# a proxy (`blocking::Dialer::stream`); a target that goes directly (the
# loopback, `NO_PROXY`) keeps podvm's direct dial, with its bound on the
# resolution. With no proxy variable, no runtime starts. The `proxy` binary
# (an SSH ProxyCommand) still dials directly. podvm-image keeps ureq and its
# own proxy rules.
# podvm's tests of podvm-ssh (with the new tests of transport/egress: a
# stand-in CONNECT proxy on the loopback for HTTPS_PROXY and ALL_PROXY, the
# loopback and NO_PROXY around it, an unusable setting refused); the
# integration test of the relay where sshd is; clippy of the workspace and
# rustfmt of the crate, as podvm's gate.yml runs them; podvm's record gate;
# each Rust toolchain of the workflows against the rust-version of
# podcrates; and the binaries `node`, `operator` and `podvm` for x86_64 musl
# (podvm's .cargo/config.toml: zig cc, static CRT), with podcrates' static
# check.
cargo test -q -p podvm-ssh --lib
if command -v sshd > /dev/null || [ -x /usr/sbin/sshd ]; then cargo test -q -p podvm-ssh --test mux_two_client; else echo "adoption: no sshd: the test mux_two_client does not run"; fi
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-ssh --check
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (pod-proxy,
# pod-term and pod-tls at 0.4.0); the trial's path form has no row for them.
# Each other row of the patch must be the generated one.
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
cargo build -q -p podvm-ssh --bin node --bin operator && cargo build -q -p podvm --bin podvm
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/node"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/operator"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm"
